---
title: Navbar
description: The bar across the top. Two arrangements of the same parts — an app bar that sits above a side nav, and a site navbar that carries the links itself — and both fold into a menu panel on a phone.
eyebrow: Navigation
source: src/layout/topbar.css · partials/shell/topbar.hbs · partials/shell/navbar.hbs
---
<h2>Site navbar</h2>
<p>For a site without a side nav. Brand, primary links and a "More" menu on the left; search, settings and a call to action on the right. It is one partial:</p>
{{#example flush=true}}
<div style="--im-gutter: 1rem">{{> "shell/navbar" id="demo" line=true}}</div>
{{/example}}
<p>The links come from Ghost's <strong>Navigation</strong> setting and the "More" menu from <strong>Secondary navigation</strong> — both rendered by <code>partials/navigation.hbs</code>. The current page is <code>aria-current="page"</code>.</p>

<h3>What happens as it narrows</h3>
<div class="im-table-scroll">
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Width</th><th>Left</th><th>Right</th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td>≥ 64rem (<code>lg</code>)</td><td>brand · links · More ▾</td><td>search · settings · CTA</td></tr>
		<tr><td>&lt; 64rem</td><td>☰ · brand</td><td>search · settings · CTA</td></tr>
		<tr><td>&lt; 40rem (<code>sm</code>)</td><td>☰ · brand</td><td>search · CTA — theme moves into the menu panel</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>☰ opens the <a href="#menu-panel">menu panel</a> holding the same primary and secondary links and the theme switch. Narrow this window to see it — or open it here:</p>
{{#example center=true}}
<button class="im-btn im-btn-outline" type="button" data-drawer-open="#demo-drawer">{{> "icons/menu"}} Open the menu panel</button>
{{/example}}

<h3>Parameters</h3>
<div class="im-table-scroll">
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Param</th><th></th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td><code>id</code></td><td>Prefix for the menu and panel ids. Default <code>"nav"</code>; only needed for two navbars on one page.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>line</code></td><td><code>true</code> — a hairline under the bar.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>cta_label</code>, <code>cta_url</code></td><td>The button. Defaults to "Subscribe" → Ghost's signup portal; hidden for signed-in members.</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h2>App bar</h2>
<p>For a layout <em>with</em> a side nav — this site. Three columns: the nav toggle and brand, a centred search, actions. The links live in the side nav, so the bar stays quiet.</p>
{{#example flush=true}}
<div style="--im-gutter: 1rem">
	<header class="im-topbar" style="position: static">
		<div class="im-topbar-start"><button class="im-btn im-btn-ghost im-btn-icon" type="button" aria-label="Collapse navigation">{{> "icons/panel-left"}}</button><a class="im-brand" href="#app-bar">Publication</a><span class="im-badge im-badge-outline">Beta</span></div>
		<div class="im-topbar-search"><button class="im-searchbar" type="button">{{> "icons/search"}}<span>Search</span><kbd>/</kbd></button></div>
		<div class="im-topbar-end"><button class="im-btn im-btn-ghost im-btn-icon" type="button" aria-label="Notifications">{{> "icons/bell"}}</button><a class="im-btn im-btn-sm im-btn-primary" href="#app-bar">Subscribe</a></div>
	</header>
</div>
{{/example}}
{{{{code "hbs"}}}}
{{#> "shell/topbar"}}
	<span class="im-badge im-badge-outline">Beta</span>      {{!-- optional: anything after the brand --}}
{{/"shell/topbar"}}
{{{{/code}}}}
<p>Below <code>md</code> the search column goes and the panel toggle becomes ☰. The search "field" is a <em>button</em> that looks like a field — it opens a dialog; with <code>data-ghost-search</code> on it, Ghost's own.</p>

<h2>Parts</h2>
<div class="im-table-scroll">
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Class</th><th></th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td><code>im-topbar</code></td><td>The bar: sticky, translucent, blurred. <code>im-topbar-site</code> for the two-column site arrangement; <code>im-topbar-line</code> for a hairline.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-topbar-start</code> · <code>-search</code> · <code>-end</code></td><td>The columns.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-brand</code></td><td>Logo image or site title.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-topbar-nav</code> · <code>im-toplink</code></td><td>Primary links; hidden below <code>lg</code>. A <code>&lt;button class="im-toplink" popovertarget="…"&gt;</code> opens a <a href="/navigation/menu/">menu</a> and its chevron turns.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-searchbar</code></td><td>The search button.</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h2>Menu panel</h2>
<p>On a phone the menu is not a drawer sliding in from the side: it is a <strong>rounded sheet that opens inside the viewport</strong>, over a blurred page, with the links as <strong>tiles in two columns</strong>. A group of links is a tile that opens across both columns; only one is open at a time.</p>
{{#example center=true}}
<button class="im-btn im-btn-primary" type="button" data-drawer-open="#panel-demo">{{> "icons/menu"}} Open a menu panel</button>
<dialog class="im-navpanel" id="panel-demo" aria-label="Menu">
	<div class="im-navpanel-head"><a class="im-brand" href="#menu-panel">{{@site.title}}</a><button class="im-btn im-btn-ghost im-btn-icon" type="button" data-drawer-close aria-label="Close">{{> "icons/x"}}</button></div>
	<nav class="im-navpanel-grid" aria-label="Demo">
		<a class="im-navtile im-navtile-stacked" href="#menu-panel" aria-current="page">{{> "icons/house"}}<span>Home</span></a>
		<a class="im-navtile im-navtile-stacked" href="#menu-panel">{{> "icons/pencil"}}<span>Writing</span></a>
		<details class="im-navtile-group" name="panel-demo">
			<summary class="im-navtile">{{> "icons/layers"}}<span>Projects</span><small>4</small></summary>
			<div class="im-navtile-items"><a href="#menu-panel">Case studies</a><a href="#menu-panel">Open source</a><a href="#menu-panel">Talks</a><a href="#menu-panel">Experiments</a></div>
		</details>
		<details class="im-navtile-group" name="panel-demo">
			<summary class="im-navtile">{{> "icons/graduation-cap"}}<span>Courses</span><small>3</small></summary>
			<div class="im-navtile-items"><a href="#menu-panel">CRM Analytics</a><a href="#menu-panel">Job seekers</a><a href="#menu-panel">Salesforce</a></div>
		</details>
		<a class="im-navtile" href="#menu-panel">{{> "icons/user"}}<span>About</span></a>
		<a class="im-navtile" href="#menu-panel">{{> "icons/mail"}}<span>Contact</span></a>
		<p class="im-caption">More</p>
		<a class="im-navtile" href="#menu-panel"><span>Newsletter</span></a>
		<a class="im-navtile" href="#menu-panel"><span>Now</span></a>
		<a class="im-navtile im-navtile-wide" href="#menu-panel">{{> "icons/rss"}}<span>RSS feed</span><small>/rss/</small></a>
	</nav>
	<div class="im-navpanel-foot">{{> "components/theme-button"}}<a class="im-btn im-btn-ghost im-btn-icon" href="#menu-panel" aria-label="GitHub">{{> "icons/brand-github"}}</a><a class="im-btn im-btn-primary im-btn-sm" style="margin-left: auto" href="#menu-panel">Subscribe</a></div>
</dialog>
{{/example}}
<div class="im-table-scroll">
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Class</th><th></th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td><code>im-navpanel</code></td><td>The sheet — a native <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code>, so the focus trap, <kbd>Esc</kbd>, the backdrop and scroll locking all come from the browser. <code>--im-navpanel-width</code> (34rem), <code>--im-navpanel-columns</code> (2; becomes 1 under 20rem).</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-navpanel-head</code> · <code>-grid</code> · <code>-foot</code></td><td>Brand and the cross; the tiles; theme, accounts and a call to action. An <code>im-caption</code> in the grid names a run of tiles.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-navtile</code></td><td>One link: optional icon, label, optional <code>&lt;small&gt;</code> count. <code>-stacked</code> puts the icon above the label, for a short menu; <code>-wide</code> spans both columns. The current page is filled with ink.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-navtile-group</code></td><td>A <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> whose <code>&lt;summary&gt;</code> is a tile. Open, it takes the whole row and lays <code>im-navtile-items</code> out in the same columns; the grid packs densely, so no cell is left empty beside it. Give the groups one shared <code>name</code> and the browser keeps only one open.</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>Any element with <code>data-drawer-open="#id"</code> opens it; <code>data-drawer-close</code>, or a click on the blurred surround, closes it. In a Ghost theme, <code>\{{navigation as="tiles"}}</code> prints the site's links as tiles — that is what <code>partials/shell/navbar.hbs</code> does.</p>

<h2>Details that matter</h2>
<ul>
	<li><strong>Which buttons show is set with utilities on the element</strong> (<code>lg:hidden</code>, <code>max-sm:hidden</code>), not in the bar's CSS — <code>im-btn</code> sets <code>display</code> in a later layer and would win.</li>
	<li><strong>Sticky offset:</strong> the bar's height is <code>--im-bar-height</code>. Anything else sticky, and <code>scroll-padding-top</code> for anchor links, is derived from it.</li>
	<li><strong>A skip link</strong> should be the first thing in <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> — see this site's layout.</li>
	<li><strong>One <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code> per set of links</strong>, each with an <code>aria-label</code>, so a screen-reader user can tell "Primary" from "More".</li>
</ul>
